<title>CANADA: Canada 1995/96 budget deficit falls to C$28.6 bln.</title>
<headline>Canada 1995/96 budget deficit falls to C$28.6 bln.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's final budget deficit for fiscal 1995/96 (April-March) was C$28.6 billion, down from the C$32.7 billion projected in the year's budget, Finance Minister Paul Martin said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Canada's budget deficit fell to C$1.88 billion in August from C$3.06 billion a year ago, according to the monthly fiscal monitor released by Canada's Finance Department.</p>
<p>Over the first five months of the fiscal year, April to August, the deficit has fallen to C$8.33 billion from C$13.69 billion in the year-earlier period.  </p>
<p>Budgetary transactions (in billions of dollars)</p>
<p>						 Aug 96     Aug 95</p>
<p>Revenues				     +9.99	+10.05</p>
<p>Deficit					 -1.88	-3.06</p>
<p>Program spending			    -8.19	-9.17</p>
<p>Operating balance			   +1.81	+0.88</p>
<p>Public debt charges			 -3.69	-3.94</p>
<p>Financial requirements (ex forex)     -0.63	-2.13</p>
<p>(Note: Positive numbers indicate net source of funds.</p>
<p>Negative numbers indicate net requirement for funds.)</p>
<p>Budgetary transactions (in billions of dollars)</p>
<p>				   Yr to date 96/97   Yr to date 95/96</p>
<p>Revenues				     +51.40     +49.03</p>
<p>Deficit					 -8.33     -13.69</p>
<p>Program spending			   -40.60     -43.07</p>
<p>Operating balance			   +10.80     +5.96</p>
<p>Public debt charges			 -19.13    -19.64</p>
<p>Financial requirements (ex forex)     -6.60     -12.67</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745</p>
